%% Swimlane view (five lanes) — From Natural-Language Request to Applied Infrastructure in Nebula
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor U as 👤 User / Human Reviewer
  participant UI as 🖥️ Nebula Web UI + Core API
  participant AG as 🤖 Nebula LLM Agents
  participant CT as ⚙️🔒 Deterministic Services + Control Gates
  participant EX as 🌐 External: Git · IaC engine · Object storage · Slack · Cloud

  rect rgb(227,242,253)
    Note over U,UI: PHASE 1–2 · Request, identity, session
    U->>UI: Describe infrastructure in natural language (wizard)
    UI->>CT: Validate OIDC bearer JWT (or dev identity) · role ≥ developer
    CT-->>UI: 401 / 403 on failure ⛔
    UI->>CT: Cloud-project preflight (authz sidecar · disabled and fail-open by default)
    UI->>EX: git ls-remote on repository
    EX-->>UI: 400 if unreachable ⛔
    UI->>CT: Create / resolve user-owned session · 202 + session id
    UI-->>U: SSE progress stream starts
    CT->>CT: Acquire in-flight guard (PostgreSQL CAS) · clone repo into ephemeral workspace · start tracing
  end

  rect rgb(243,229,245)
    Note over AG,CT: PHASE 3–4 · Filter and compose (small model)
    CT->>AG: Request Filter Agent — is the request acceptable? (status FILTERING)
    alt not acceptable
      AG-->>UI: rationale → session UNCOMPLETED 🟧
      UI-->>U: reformulate the request
    else acceptable
      CT->>AG: Prompt Compositor — pick relevant templates, conventions, guidelines (Phoenix)
    end
  end

  rect rgb(241,248,233)
    Note over AG,EX: PHASE 5 · Generate → Validate → Correct (≤ 5 iterations)
    loop up to 5 validation iterations
      CT->>AG: Infrastructure Generation Agent (main model, ≤ 70 tool calls, ends via task_complete)
      AG->>CT: files edited in workspace
      CT->>EX: store per-file changes · commit + push session branch
      CT->>AG: Session Target Generator (main model) → -target list
      CT->>EX: IaC sidecar: init → validate → plan -target (async jobs, polled)
      EX-->>CT: plan result or engine errors
      alt engine errors and iterations left
        CT-->>AG: feed errors back to the generator 🔁
      else 5 iterations exhausted
        CT-->>UI: session FAILED (422) · problem summary 🟥
      end
    end
  end

  rect rgb(255,248,225)
    Note over AG,EX: PHASE 6 · Implicit drift pre-check on the validated targets (≤ 2 rounds)
    loop up to 2 rounds
      CT->>EX: plan + show -json on the session's targets
      EX-->>CT: plan JSON → DeepDiff → inverted drift operations · artifacts stored
      alt plan shows differences
        CT->>AG: Drift Task Splitter (small) → plain-language operations
        CT->>AG: Reconciliation Filter (small) — reads diff_history, drops ops that undo the session's own changes
        alt genuine drift remains
          CT->>AG: batches of ≤ 8 ops re-enter the generation loop 🔁
        else only the session's own changes
          CT->>CT: stop · plan is final
        end
      else clean plan
        CT->>CT: stop · resources in sync
      end
    end
  end

  rect rgb(232,245,233)
    Note over AG,EX: PHASE 7 · Report and artifacts
    CT->>AG: Report Generator (main model)
    CT->>EX: report · plan · drift JSON · code changes → object storage (metadata in PostgreSQL)
    EX-->>UI: presigned URLs for the UI
  end

  rect rgb(255,243,224)
    Note over AG,EX: PHASE 8 · Independent compliance audit → verdict computed in code
    alt compliance checker enabled (deployment config)
      CT->>AG: Compliance Auditor (small, read-only tools) audits the report → report_compliance_findings
      AG-->>CT: structured findings (rule id, severity, resource, message, fix)
    else disabled
      CT->>CT: empty passing report
    end
    CT->>CT: 🔒 VERDICT: any ERROR/CRITICAL ⇒ fail (model's own "passed" ignored) · plan pinned either way
    alt fail
      CT->>CT: sessions.is_blocked = true
      CT-)EX: iac.compliance.check_failed → Slack (fire-and-forget) 🔔
      CT-->>UI: 🟥 apply and PR merge will answer 409 · PR creation still allowed
    else pass
      CT->>CT: sessions.is_blocked = false
      CT-->>UI: 🟩 generated and validated — awaiting human apply
    end
  end

  rect rgb(250,250,250)
    Note over U,EX: PHASE 9 · Optional pull request and human review
    opt user requests a PR
      U->>UI: PUT /repository/pr
      CT->>AG: PR Title & Description Agent (small)
      CT->>EX: Git provider adapter creates the PR (GitHub / Azure DevOps / GitLab)
      EX-->>U: 🟨 awaiting review — code, plan, drift, compliance report, cost, CI
      alt changes requested / conflict / CI failure
        U->>UI: revision instructions → new round in the same session 🔁 (back to phase 3)
      else approved
        U->>UI: PUT /repository/pr/merge (409 if is_blocked)
        UI->>EX: merge into default branch
      else rejected / closed
        U-->>UI: 🟥 delivery stops · history kept
      end
    end
  end

  rect rgb(232,245,233)
    Note over U,EX: PHASE 10 · Human-triggered apply (never automatic)
    U->>UI: POST /iac/apply — explicit human action
    UI->>CT: 🔒 authenticated · developer role · owner · not blocked · pinned generate plan · guard free
    CT-->>U: ⛔ 401 / 403 / 409 (locked, or no pinned plan e.g. drift-only session)
    CT->>EX: IaC sidecar: ONE apply of the pinned plan (no re-plan, no retry)
    alt success
      EX-->>CT: applied
      CT->>AG: Report Generator → apply report
      CT-->>U: 🟩 Infrastructure applied · session COMPLETED
      Note over EX: ☁️ cloud reaches the requested state
    else failure
      CT->>AG: Report Generator → apply failure report
      CT-)EX: iac.apply.failure → Slack 🔔
      CT-->>U: 🟥 session FAILED · no automatic retry · new generate round needed
    end
    CT->>CT: pinned plan discarded · workspace cleaned · in-flight guard released (finally)
  end
